# 04 - LED-wave

## Objective

Create a smooth wave animation using 5 LEDs.

## Components Used

- ESP32
- 5 LED
- 5 220 Ω resistor
- Breadboard
- Jumper wires

## Concepts

- for loops
- HIGH and LOW states
- pinMode()
- digitalWrite()
- delay()
- variables

## Wiring

|   LED   |               ESP32              |
|---------|----------------------------------|
| Anode   | GPIO 23 (through 220 Ω resistor) |
| Cathode | GND                              |

## Expected Result

The LEDs display a smooth wave animation going from LED1 (right LED) to LED5 (left LED)

## What I Learned

- Sequential logic
- How current flows through an LED
- Why a resistor is required
- How the Arduino loop() function works
- How to properly use variables
- How to use delays properly

## Challenges

- Forgot to set the pin as OUTPUT.

## Resources

- ESP32 Documentation
- Arduino Documentation

